        "comments": "The assembly iHelSar1.1 is based on 50x PacBio data, 294x coverage 10X Genomics Chromium data, and 111x coverage Dovetail Genomics Hi-C data from a different individual iHelSar2 (BioSample SAMEA8947139) generated at the Wellcome Sanger Institute. The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with wtdbg2, retained haplotig identification with Purge Haplotigs, 10X based scaffolding with scaff10x, Arrow polishing, and two rounds of FreeBayes polishing. The assembly was analysed and manually improved using gEVAL, Hi-C based scaffolding was carried out with SALSA2, and finally there was another round of manual curation. Chromosome-scale scaffolds are named by synteny to the Heliconius melpomene melpomene assembly Hmel2.5 in LepBase.",
